  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="13">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Iudex">Iudex</ref> 13</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-g-a">Yfelra gerefena þeaw ýs, þæt hí nymað ælcwiht ⁊ uneaðe hí þam þearfiendum lytles hwæt læfa[ð].</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-q">Malorum prepositorum mos est, ut quicquid possunt auferant et uix necessariorum parum quid relinquant sustentationum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#unattributed" corresp="#wit-g-a">It is the custom of evil officials that they take everything and unwillingly leave little for the poor</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Böser Amtleute Brauch ist, dass sie jegliches fortnehmen und kaum etwas weniges den armen [Hintersassen ihres Bezirks] belassen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">It is the custom of bad reeves that they take away everything and scarcely leave a little to the needy [tenants of their district].</ab>
        <note type="editorial">The ‘ð’ of ‘læfa[ð]’ was cut off in binding.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
